From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] RenderManager: present the prepared picture when it is due,
 not a refresh early

A frame due within a refresh may be flipped early. The picture a start or
resume was prepared on went out that way: one refresh before its time,
then the next frame waited for its own slot, and the prepared picture was
on screen twice - one repeated frame at every start and resume.

Present the prepared picture only once it is due.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
@@ -1520,7 +1520,9 @@ void CRenderManager::PrepareNextRender()
 
     m_playerPort->UpdateRenderBuffers(m_queued.size(), m_discard.size(), m_free.size());
   }
-  else if (!combined && renderPts > (nextFramePts - frametime))
+  // Never for the picture a start or resume was prepared on: flipped a refresh
+  // early it is shown twice while the next one waits for its own slot.
+  else if (!combined && !firstPrerollPicture && renderPts > (nextFramePts - frametime))
   {
     m_lateframes = 0;
     m_presentstep = PRESENT_FLIP;
